{
 "about": "Concurrency conformance scenarios of the precondition model (spec R60; section 14 R62: written in proto_db only, protoBaseST runs them after its port). Data only: tests/conformance/test_concurrency_scenarios.py executes them through proto_db in standalone, group-commit and cluster mode.",
 "notation": {
  "scenario": "name; row (one of rows); base; a and b, the operations of transactions A and B, both opened on the base and run A then B; order, the commit order; expect: state (the final state) or conflict (the unit the second commit raises ProtoConflictError on; only the fields given are compared). note: a comment.",
  "state": "{roots: {name: root}, mutables: {name: value}}; a root is {value: v} (an object root holding a plain value), {dictionary: {k: v}}, {hash_dictionary: {k: v}}, {set: [e]}, {counted_set: [[e, n]]}, {rkd: [[k, [record]]]}, {list: [v]}; a collection may add indexes: [kind], kind 'equality' (index 'e') or 'range' (index 'r'), both over the element (KeySpec.element()). Lists in a state are sorted, except a list root's items.",
  "operations": "[set_root, n, root], [remove_root, n], [get_root, n], [root_names], [new_mutable, n, v], [set_mutable, n, v], [remove_mutable, n], [get_mutable, n], [mutable_names], [write, root, method, args...] (the version the method returns is assigned to the root: set_at, remove_at, add, remove, union, difference, intersection, remove_record, remove_key, append_last, append_first, extend, insert_at, slice, add_index kind, remove_index kind), [read, root, method, args...] (get_at, get, has, count_of, len, count, items, elements, keys, key_at_position, position_of, index_names, get_index kind, lookup v (an equality query), greater_than v (a range query), scan (a query without a term))",
  "conflict": "{kind, root, key[, index]} (a range has no key): kind is the unit class (root, root_presence, root_names, cell, cell_names, key, element, count, records, position, whole, index_defs, index_group, range); root is null for cells and the name sets; key is the cell name for a cell."
 },
